When working on UI, design, layout, or frontend visual refinement:

## Authority (mandatory before edits)

1. [`architecture/frontend-ui-ux/governance/CANONICAL_AUTHORITY_MAP.md`](../../architecture/frontend-ui-ux/governance/CANONICAL_AUTHORITY_MAP.md)
2. [`architecture/frontend-ui-ux/governance/FIGMA_AND_VISUAL_PRECEDENCE.md`](../../architecture/frontend-ui-ux/governance/FIGMA_AND_VISUAL_PRECEDENCE.md)
3. [`architecture/frontend-ui-ux/design-system/SHARED_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`](../../architecture/frontend-ui-ux/design-system/SHARED_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md)
4. Relevant product authority under `architecture/frontend-ui-ux/products/`

## Figma

- **Default contract:** registered FEUX architecture + implemented tokens — not unconditional Figma SSOT.
- On **owner-approved redesign** tasks: use the Figma MCP server to inspect the named artifact.
- Treat the **codebase** as source of truth for **functionality**.
- Do not remove code-only functional UI because Figma omits it.
- Visually harmonize code-only elements to the **current** design language (L0–L4, tokens).
- If Figma and implementation disagree and the task is not an approved redesign: document the conflict; verify intended target — do not invent design intent.
- Preserve responsiveness, dark/light mode, shell behavior, and component consistency.
- Refactor existing pages/components instead of regenerating entire screens when possible.

## Prohibited

- Creating a parallel design system without owner approval.
- Treating `docs/ui/*` (2026-08 pack) or `frontend/figma-*` stubs as current authority.